{
  "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
  "reason": "The script accurately depicts the described night harbor sequence across S009-S011, including flare discharge into fuel-soaked blankets, vessel diesel fire, mortar fireworks, anchor line parting, Mara diving into cold night water to swim a line to a mooring buoy, boat maneuvering near flames, and a skiff carrying Sam and a dog. The cited CSATF Safety Bulletins (#16, #17, #15, #6) and Actsafe Bulletin #17 support the recommended pyrotechnic operator/permits, water safety devices/accounting, hypothermia mitigation, marine/water coordination, and conditional animal/minor safeguards.",
  "failure_mode": "none",
  "claim_checks": [
    {
      "field": "finding",
      "quote": "Scenes S009, S010, and S011 depict a heavily stacked sequence of physical hazards taking place in open harbor waters at night. The staged action includes discharging a flare gun into fuel-soaked blankets on an anchored vessel (Margaret Rose), causing an engulfing fire and diesel burn, adjacent aerial mortar fireworks launched from the seawall, a severed anchor line causing the burning vessel to drift toward moored floats, a character (Mara) diving into cold water at night to swim a line to a mooring buoy, boat maneuvers adjacent to flames to tow the vessel, and an adjacent skiff carrying a child character (Sam) and a dog (Barnacle).",
      "basis": "script",
      "status": "SUPPORTED",
      "reason": "Accurately summarizes the depicted action and events in scenes S009, S010, and S011.",
      "citation_numbers": [],
      "support_spans": [],
      "script_spans": [
        "Mara stands, braces, and fires the flare into the soaked blankets amidships.\n\nWHUMP. A line of blue-orange flame walks the deck like it knows the boat. Then the diesel catches and the MARGARET ROSE goes up -- a column of fire standing on the black water, doubled in the swell, huge.",
        "Crow touches a road flare to the mortar fuse. The Fourth of July stash goes up -- white and gold chrysanthemums blooming over the burning boat, reflections shattering across the harbor.",
        "The anchor line, burned through at the chock, parts. The burning boat swings free and begins to drift, slow and terrible, on the last of the tide.\n\nToward a row of moored floats.",
        "Before Danny can speak she has the spare line over her shoulder and she DIVES -- off the skiff into the black water, surfacing in the firelight, swimming hard for the mooring buoy off the Margaret Rose's bow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "field": "finding",
      "quote": "While the script depicts these story events, practical versus visual effects execution, shooting jurisdiction, casting ages, and marine safety protocols remain unconfirmed production decisions.",
